{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it was on the day Moses finished.</b> Above he explained the service of the Kohathites, carried on the shoulder; now he explains the service of the Gershonites and Merarites, which cannot be carried on the shoulder but only on wagons. And the section of the dedication of the altar was juxtaposed to the section of the priests, to teach that on the day Aaron lifted his hands to bless the people, afterward on that very day the dedication of the altar began." "<b>And he anointed it.</b> And thereby <b>he sanctified it.</b> So too our Rabbis said: all the vessels that Moses made — their anointing sanctified them. From this point onward, their use in service dedicated them."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:48.385566530Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}